# Build context is the repository root. Keeping node_modules, bin/ and obj/ out of it
# is the difference between a context of a few MB and one of several hundred: the
# Angular client's node_modules alone is ~400 MB, and the node stage in
# src/API.Web/Dockerfile installs its own from package-lock.json anyway.
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.angular
**/.classpath
**/.project
**/.settings
**/.toolstarget
**/*.*proj.user
**/*.dbmdl
**/*.jfm
**/azds.yaml
**/bin
**/obj
**/charts
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log
**/secrets.dev.yaml
**/values.dev.yaml
**/Dockerfile*
**/docker-compose*
src/API.Web/ClientApp/dist
src/API.Web/ClientApp/out-tsc

# Never let a real secret into a build context.
**/.env
!**/.env.template
**/Common.env
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/*.pfx
**/ssl/*.key

LICENSE
README.md
docs
PORTFOLIO-PLAN.md
